<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RUT_BlueDesert                                UtinniPatches · authored 2026-09-09
    Full sheet: design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/the_blue_desert.md (FROZEN,
    BIOME_FREEZE_FABLE_REVIEW_1). Replaces the donor GRiNDTerra Biomes def
    BiomeGRimond ("Blue desert") on the 1,029 tiles it currently holds — own def,
    not a patch, same shape of decision as RUT_NightsideIce (§0 of that sheet):
    the donor ships an ordinary Earth-desert zoo and water-based flora wired onto
    a biome the sheet hard-bans that content from (§6.1 "No water-based plants or
    animals"; §0 "Evicted wholesale: the entire Earth desert zoo... and grimpepper
    and every water-based plant"). Patching all of that out across MayRequire
    branches is silent-failure territory; restating the shape directly is not.

    🔴 NOT ParentName="BiomeGRimond" for the same engine reason RUT_NightsideIce
    documents against ParentName="IceSheet": ParentName only resolves against a
    Name="..." XML attribute, and small third-party biome defs routinely carry
    none. Modeled instead on RUT_NightsideIce's own proven shape — both are
    frigid (-42.6°C median vs -33.8°C), zero-water, ice-ground biomes on this
    same frozen nightside, so its shape is a better template than the donor's.

    MEASURED (sheet §0, off world/ASHKARR_WORLDMAP_tiles.csv): 1,029 tiles, temp
    median -42.6°C (range -58...-19.4, summer max below 0°C on every tile),
    zero water, zero rivers, rolling plateau. Sheet's own donor-inventory read:
    animal density 0.5 ("the sparsest def defined"), plant density 0.33,
    movement 1.5, disease clock 90 days — movement and disease clock kept below
    since they don't depend on undesigned content; animal/plant density zeroed
    for now, same restraint RUT_NightsideIce used, because the sheet's actual
    fauna (Swallowers, Burners, Pickers) and flora (transparent fractal ferns/
    dandelions/fuzzballs) are explicitly still owed (§"Owed" — NEW-ART ledger),
    not invented here.

    Weather: ONLY Clear authored. The sheet names three more (The Haze, ice-sand
    drift re-skinning BlueSnow, ice fog re-skinning Blue Fogstorm/Purple Fog)
    but its own "Owed" section lists all three as still needing an "engine
    feasibility pass" — they do not exist as WeatherDefs yet, ours or the
    donor's re-skinned. Same restraint RUT_NightsideIce applied to its own
    margin events (ablation drift, rime-fall, thaw pulse): named in the sheet,
    not invented in this def. Zeroed explicitly rather than left absent, so a
    later MayRequire audit sees a deliberate 0, not a silent gap.

    Terrain: Ice (vanilla), matching the sheet's own "the ground is ancient
    water ice; the sand is ice; the snow is sand" — real ice-sand terrain art
    is separately unowed work, same placeholder pattern as RUT_NightsideIce's
    texture note below.

    NOT this item's scope (sheet's own §0 lobe-mosaic ruling and Owed list):
    painting the def onto the 1,029 tiles currently holding BiomeGRimond (a
    live-world edit needing the bridge and an owner-reviewed worldview.py
    render first, same two-step shape as HORRORWASTES_BIOME_DISSOLVE_1 —
    filed separately as BLUE_DESERT_WORLD_SWITCH_1); the lobe-mosaic anti-
    bullseye repaint (§0); The Haze/ice-sand-drift/ice-fog WeatherDefs;
    blue ice as a mineable resource (WATER_KINDS_TAXONOMY_1's distilled-purity
    row); the quarry injection templates and crysalis trigger mechanism
    (HORRORS_RAIDING_FACTION_1); §6.5's ruling that Bluefire Mountains
    (BiomeGRimphire) is never used — a painting-pass constraint, not a field
    here.

    BLUE_DESERT_LIFE_AUTHORING_1 (2026-09-21): the dorrak (Swallower), krissek
    (Burner), vekkit (Picker) and the transparent fractal flora (palefloss/
    glassfern/chimeglobe) are now built (ThingDefs_Races/RM_BlueDesertFauna.xml,
    ThingDefs_Plants/RM_BlueDesertFlora.xml) and wired below, with the sheet's
    own donor-read densities (0.5/0.33) restored in the same change — this def
    is no longer sterile-by-design. See that item and the design brief
    (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/creatures/blue_desert_hydrocarbon_life.md) for
    the mechanics.
  -->

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>RUT_BlueDesert</defName>
    <label>the Blue Desert</label>
    <description>From orbit the bluest thing on the planet; underfoot, colorless. A plateau of the oldest ice on Ash'karr, its "sand" ice grain, its "snow" that same sand blowing, scoured bare by cold wind draining off higher ground. Nothing here runs on water: what lives is a fuel charge stable only in the cold, and warmth is detonation. It is usually clear, silent, and almost empty — then the ablation line gives something up.</description>
    <workerClass>BiomeWorker_IceSheet</workerClass>
    <settleWarning>The Blue Desert is a hydrocarbon-ice plateau with no water-based life and no soil. Everything native here is a cold-stable fuel charge that detonates on warming — mining and heating are both a hazard, not just a convenience.</settleWarning>
    <!-- allowRoads true per the standing owner ruling (RUT_NightsideIce's own comment, 2026-09-07): "All of our biomes should allow roads." -->
    <allowRoads>true</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>false</allowRivers>
    <allowFarmingCamps>false</allowFarmingCamps>
    <isExtremeBiome>true</isExtremeBiome>
    <!-- BLUE_DESERT_LIFE_AUTHORING_1 (2026-09-21): restored to the sheet's own
         donor-read numbers now that the cast exists (RM_Dorrak/RM_Krissek/
         RM_Vekkit below, and completelyIgnoreFertility flora that actually
         makes plantDensity mean something on Ice — §1a of the design brief). -->
    <animalDensity>0.5</animalDensity>
    <plantDensity>0.33</plantDensity>
    <!-- wildPlants: the owner's 2026-09-10 sheet moved AB_CrystalHorn/AB_ToxiGrass/
         PoisonPlantTallGrass here (SHEET_ORPHAN_CONSUMPTION_1, owner review 2026-09-20,
         "propane lakes and blue desert only" / "blue desert rare"). Those three rows
         landed in rosters/the_blue_desert.json and reached the game only through
         `BiomeFlora_Ashkarr.xml`'s replace operation, which this element existed purely
         as an anchor for. That operation is retired for biomes whose BiomeDef we author
         (BIOMEFLORA_PATCH_WIPES_WILDPLANTS_1), so the rows are written out here instead.
         Left as-is per BLUE_DESERT_LIFE_AUTHORING_1's own §10 (item's default: "leave
         them as they are; plantDensity restore makes them live too once our plants set
         the map's completelyIgnoreFertility flag" — not a ruling on whether a
         water-metabolism donor plant belongs in a ban-1 biome, which stays open for the
         owner). RM_Palefloss/RM_Glassfern/RM_Chimeglobe are the biome's own ratified
         flora (design brief §6) added alongside them, not a replacement for them. -->
    <wildPlants>
      <AB_ToxiGrass>0.6</AB_ToxiGrass>  <!-- toxigrass -->
      <AB_CrystalHorn>0.4</AB_CrystalHorn>  <!-- crystal horn -->
      <PoisonPlantTallGrass>0.4</PoisonPlantTallGrass>  <!-- poison tall grass -->
      <RM_Palefloss>1.0</RM_Palefloss>
      <RM_Glassfern>0.5</RM_Glassfern>
      <RM_Chimeglobe>0.25</RM_Chimeglobe>
    </wildPlants>
    <hasVirtualPlants>false</hasVirtualPlants>
    <forageability>0</forageability>
    <movementDifficulty>1.5</movementDifficulty>
    <lakeBeachTerrain>Ice</lakeBeachTerrain>
    <mudTerrain>Ice</mudTerrain>
    <texture>World/Biomes/IceSheet</texture> <!-- placeholder, per RUT_NightsideIce's own note; the sheet's real "extremely blue from far away" art is separate, unowed work -->
    <diseaseMtbDays>90</diseaseMtbDays>
    <diseases>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Flu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Plague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
    </diseases>
    <terrainsByFertility>
      <li>
        <terrain>Ice</terrain>
        <min>-999</min>
        <max>999</max>
      </li>
    </terrainsByFertility>
    <baseWeatherCommonalities>
      <Clear>100</Clear>
      <Fog>0</Fog>
      <Rain>0</Rain>
      <DryThunderstorm>0</DryThunderstorm>
      <RainyThunderstorm>0</RainyThunderstorm>
      <FoggyRain>0</FoggyRain>
      <SnowGentle>0</SnowGentle>
      <SnowHard>0</SnowHard>
      <GrayPall MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Anomaly">0</GrayPall>
      <Windy MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0</Windy>
      <Overcast MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0</Overcast>
      <Blizzard MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0</Blizzard>
    </baseWeatherCommonalities>
    <!-- BLUE_DESERT_LIFE_AUTHORING_1 (2026-09-21): the three resident fauna the sheet
         ratifies (§3-§5 of the design brief) — superseding the prior "STAYS EMPTY"
         ruling from BIOME_FAUNA_ASSIGNMENT_SITTING_1, which was correct only until
         these defs existed. Commonalities per brief §6c: vekkit most common (herd
         scavenger), dorrak mid (slow, armoured), krissek least common (a hazard, not
         a background animal). The roster's two owner-ruled Star Wars rows (Vapaad,
         AA_Thunderbeast) ride the Utinni patch layer, not this element (§0c/§6c of the
         brief) — not added here, that is a separate wire-up. -->
    <wildAnimals>
      <RM_Vekkit>0.8</RM_Vekkit>
      <RM_Dorrak>0.5</RM_Dorrak>
      <RM_Krissek>0.35</RM_Krissek>
    </wildAnimals>
    <coastalWildAnimals />
    <allowedPackAnimals />
  </BiomeDef>

</Defs>
